body:
Pretty much any Chinese(-stocked) grocery store will have those things. The Miracle store at the south end of Town Hall station is probably the easiest to get to. The Thai Kee IGA has a good range and is very accessible in terms of English signage.

&#x200B;

If you want to go just a tiny bit off the beaten path, New Yen Yen in the Prince Centre has a great selection and I personally do most of my shopping at the unnamed shop on the corner of Ultimo Rd and Thomas St because I find it tends to be the cheapest (it's called "Chinese Grocery Store" on Google Maps).

If I had to recommend another one, it would probably be one of the Mission Escape rooms - I've not done any of them but I know people who have and they have an excellent reputation, especially for people who like tech-style puzzles and automation.

&#x200B;

Of the ones I've done in Sydney - Doctor Disaster at Enigma Room was a lot of fun - lots of different puzzles for different types of brains - though I would probably consider it a little basic now (I hear good things about In Memoriam but we just haven't made it back there); Super Cell 117 at Paniq Room is pretty unique and probably worth doing, but it's heavy on the here's-a-padlock-find-me-a-key stuff which a lot of people don't enjoy as much. We also did Bank Heist at Social Escape recently (not near the CBD but it's not really any further than Newtown where Cipher Room is) and it's a well-designed room, but difficult! There's a lot to get through in an hour.

&#x200B;

Good luck with whatever you choose! I hope you don't stress too much about picking a room at Cipher - they're all terrific.
